<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Murad Khan Zand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1781">1781</a>–<a href="/years/1785">1785</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Ali Murad Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Murad Khan Zand was a ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the years after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan Zand</a> in 1779. He deposed Karim Khan's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-fath-khan-zand">Abu al-Fath Khan</a> and fought rival claimants for the throne. His rule was part of the prolonged succession struggle that weakened the Zand Empire and assisted the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a>.</p></div>
